WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.560
2014's Interstellar unfolds in a dystopian
version of the year 2067 in which Earth is

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.990
rapidly becoming uninhabitable thanks to climate
change.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:14.070
A group of astronauts travel to a wormhole
near Saturn in hopes of finding a new home

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.330
for humanity.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.250
Former NASA pilot Joseph Cooper leads the
team of researchers on the mission through

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.250
the wormhole.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.279
The mission doesn't exactly go the way they
planned, but don't worry -- this is a Christopher

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:28.320
Nolan movie, so you don't have to stress about
everything making perfect sense.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.050
"They constructed this three-dimensional space
inside their five-dimensional reality to allow

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.310
you to understand it."

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.560
"Well, that ain't workin'."

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.680
Cooper's daughter, Murphy, often called "Murph,"
is played by Jessica Chastain in adulthood.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.170
Murph becomes a NASA scientist herself as
the story unfolds, but at the beginning of

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:48.300
the film, before Cooper has taken off on his
mission, she's still just a kid.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.440
Since Hollywood de-aging software isn't quite
ready for primetime, the 10-year-old version

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.030
of Murph is played by another talented actress:
Mackenzie Foy.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:59.830
The young Murph doesn't just dazzle with her
heartbreaking portrayal of a young girl about

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:04.500
to lose her father in act one — she also
makes a surprise return in act three, long

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.350
after Chastain has picked up the character's
mantle.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:11.680
By the time Foy appeared in Interstellar,
she had already become somewhat recognizable

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.309
from her role in the final two Twilight films,
Breaking Dawn – Part 1 and Breaking Dawn

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.429
– Part 2.

00:01:17.429 --> 00:01:21.710
Additionally, she played Cindy Perron in The
Conjuring, one of the kids living in a haunted

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.159
Rhode Island farmhouse.

00:01:23.159 --> 00:01:24.969
But what about since Interstellar?

00:01:24.969 --> 00:01:29.380
While some child stars fizzle out in their
teen years, Foy is still shining brightly.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:33.549
While she hasn't appeared in anything as widely
recognizable as Interstellar, Foy's acting

00:01:33.549 --> 00:01:36.829
credits since the 2014 film include a couple
lead roles.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:42.119
In 2018, Foy landed the lead role of Princess
Clara in Disney's The Nutcracker and the Four

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:43.119
Realms.

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:47.549
The high-profile fantasy treatment of the
classic tale was announced in March 2016,

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:52.039
and Foy joined that summer alongside Kiera
Knightley, Helen Mirren, and Morgan Freeman

00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:54.299
— very accomplished company for the up-and-comer.

00:01:54.299 --> 00:01:58.780
Unfortunately, The Nutcracker and the Four
Realms was a flop with both critics and at

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.780
the box office.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:03.579
The film's shortcomings shouldn't be attributed
to Foy's performance, however.

00:02:03.579 --> 00:02:06.420
As Allison Rose of FlickDirect pointed out
in her review,

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:11.039
"Mackenzie Foy does a very good job as the
smart and beautiful Clara and offers a believable

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:13.180
performance as this iconic character."

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.180
"Thank you."

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:19.110
That seems to be the consensus — a capable
young actress in an otherwise mishandled film.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:23.060
As a result, Foy moved onward and upward from
the project, even appearing in yet another

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:28.250
Disney film just two years after The Nutcracker's
debut -- a modern retelling of Black Beauty.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:33.510
The classic 1877 novel about a girl and her
horse by English author Anna Sewell has been

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.010
a part of pop culture for decades.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:40.189
It's been adapted for film eight times — and
twice rendered into episodic format for British

00:02:40.189 --> 00:02:41.189
TV.

00:02:41.189 --> 00:02:44.430
The most recent attempt at a feature length
treatment found Mackenzie Foy in the lead

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.030
role of Jo Green.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.760
Disney updates the story a smidge to the present
day.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:53.110
Despite the time displacement, many of the
important details from Sewell's novel are

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.110
still present.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:58.670
Jo is still a young girl who forms a close
bond with narrator and titular Black Beauty,

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.980
in this version characterized as a wild mustang.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:05.960
Though Foy claims top human billing, Beauty
is really the star of this adaptation, and

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:10.185
as such the horse has a properly famous actor
giving voice to its equine narration: Kate

00:03:10.185 --> 00:03:11.185
Winslet.

00:03:11.185 --> 00:03:16.189
"I knew that if Jo could feel the wind in
her mane, it would help her to heal."

00:03:16.189 --> 00:03:21.189
The film was supposed to have a theatrical
release in 2020, but the COVID-19 pandemic

00:03:21.189 --> 00:03:25.689
put a damper on those plans, and Black Beauty
ended up going straight to Disney+, where

00:03:25.689 --> 00:03:27.060
it's currently streaming.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:31.209
Critics were a little kinder to Black Beauty
than they were to Foy's prior Disney adventure,

00:03:31.209 --> 00:03:32.920
The Nutcracker and the Four Realms.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:38.340
The equine escapade earned a 48 percent critical
consensus on Rotten Tomatoes, with one critic

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.939
summing it up as, quote, "mostly pleasing."

00:03:40.939 --> 00:03:45.730
That might not be a clear-cut whinny, but
it's far from a neigh.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:49.959
Mackenzie Foy isn't going anywhere anytime
soon, and you'll no doubt see her on the big

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:52.239
screen again before you know it.

